{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>For our good all the days, to keep us alive, as this day.</b> This means: we shall be those who inherit all the days, which are the life of the World to Come. And this matter is a reply to the foolishness and lack of understanding of the sectarians who ask Israel: why did Moses not state explicitly in his words to Israel that they would inherit the Garden of Eden and the bringing of the World to Come if they fulfill the Torah? A reply to their words: here he explicitly mentioned the reward of the World to Come. And the reason he did not promise them in many places anything but the Land and the tranquility of this world — that was in order to convey to them something equally accessible to all people, to women and to children, to the wise and to the unwise, in order to draw their hearts toward fear of Heaven. And likewise for this reason Moses our teacher did not warn Israel of the punishment of Gehinnom if they do not keep the commandments of the Torah, but warned them of the punishment of this-worldly life, as is explicitly stated in the section of Bechukotai and in the section of Ki Tavo and in several other places."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:03.171292914Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}